WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.140
Most AI coding tools want you to trust a server you don't control.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.812
This one doesn't ask you to.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:13.576
localagent is a local-first coding agent that actually gets things done.

00:00:13.576 --> 00:00:18.144
Bring your own model: an embedded GGUF file, Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM,

00:00:18.144 --> 00:00:22.315
or a cloud API with your own key, and you get a complete agent.

00:00:22.315 --> 00:00:26.419
It reads your code, proposes changes, and checks its own work.

00:00:26.419 --> 00:00:28.074
No telemetry, no account,

00:00:28.074 --> 00:00:33.436
and nothing leaves your machine unless you point it at a cloud provider yourself.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.847
Pick a workspace, pick a model: a tiny local model for offline work,

00:00:39.847 --> 00:00:45.744
a custom model straight from Hugging Face, or Claude, OpenAI, and Gemini with your own key.

00:00:45.744 --> 00:00:46.457
Then start.

00:00:46.457 --> 00:00:49.178
Every tab keeps its own provider and mode,

00:00:49.178 --> 00:00:53.650
so you can run a careful cloud session next to a throwaway local one.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.558
Send a task and watch the loop: read, act, check.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:02.771
Every file write shows you the exact diff before anything touches disk.

00:01:02.771 --> 00:01:04.314
You approve what you want.

00:01:04.314 --> 00:01:06.806
This isn't the model guessing what's safe.

00:01:06.806 --> 00:01:09.654
It's a deterministic permission engine deciding.

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:17.300
Four modes, plain code rules, not model judgment: ask every time, auto-accept edits,

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.605
auto-accept only what's provably safe, or plan first, read-only.

00:01:21.605 --> 00:01:23.959
And every task gets one checkpoint.

00:01:23.959 --> 00:01:29.946
If it goes sideways, revert, and your workspace is exactly how it was before you hit Run.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.644
Add your own tools over MCP.

00:01:33.644 --> 00:01:37.213
Sign in with Google and your sessions sync across machines.

00:01:37.213 --> 00:01:40.358
Switch providers mid-project without losing history.

00:01:40.358 --> 00:01:41.931
This isn't a model runner.

00:01:41.931 --> 00:01:45.681
It's the agent layer on top of whichever model you trust most.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:52.495
Run graphify on a codebase and it builds a real knowledge graph: what calls what,

00:01:52.495 --> 00:01:56.894
which files cluster together, the connections a file tree never shows you.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:01:59.663
localagent.

00:01:59.663 --> 00:02:02.402
Free, local-first, no account required.

00:02:02.402 --> 00:02:06.406
Download it for Mac or Windows, and bring your own model.

